# WebNet tutorial example - mixed TS, GNSS, and leveling on a projected grid
# Recommended for the beginner walkthrough in docs/USER_GUIDE.md.
# Workflow: open this file, confirm Project Options -> Adjustment settings,
# run Adjust, then review Adjustment Report / Processing Summary /
# Industry Standard Output / Map & Ellipses.

.3D
.UNITS M
.ORDER EN
.CRS GRID CA_NAD83_CSRS_NB_STEREO_DOUBLE
.GRID
.AMODE ANGLE
.DELTA OFF

I TS1 Tutorial-TS 0.001 1.0 1.0 1.0 0.002 0.002
I GPS1 Tutorial-GNSS 0.5 0.002 2.0 0.010 4.0
I LEV1 Tutorial-Level 0.0 0.000 0.0 0.000 0.7
.I TS1

# Fixed projected control (E, N, H)
C C1 2505000.000 7505000.000 50.000 ! ! !
C C2 2505200.000 7505015.000 50.500 ! ! !
C C3 2505105.000 7505195.000 49.700 ! ! !

# Unknown station with approximate coordinates
C U1 2505111.100 7505092.200 50.100

# Total station measurements (angle, slope distance, zenith)
M C1-C2-U1 324-27-49.0 144.270 089-55-13.6 2.0 0.004 6.0 1.600/1.500
M C2-C3-U1 338-46-22.5 118.103 090-08-43.8 2.0 0.004 6.0 1.580/1.500
M C3-C1-U1 328-27-48.9 102.765 089-43-16.0 2.0 0.004 6.0 1.620/1.500

# GNSS vectors (dE, dN)
G GPS1 C1 U1 110.8005 92.3998 0.010 0.010
G GPS1 C2 U1 -89.1995 77.3998 0.012 0.012
G GPS1 C3 U1 5.8005 -102.6002 0.010 0.010

# Differential leveling (dH, run length km, sigma mm/km)
L LEV1 C1 U1 0.3024 0.14 0.7
L LEV1 U1 C2 0.1976 0.12 0.7
L LEV1 C2 C1 -0.5000 0.26 0.7
L LEV1 C3 U1 0.6024 0.10 0.7
L LEV1 C2 C3 -0.8000 0.21 0.7
